# Cursor routing rule — historical personal copy

This repository is not canonical. For every Berkah POS task, switch to https://github.com/berkah-pos/Berkahtigaputeri and read its [AGENTS.md](https://github.com/berkah-pos/Berkahtigaputeri/blob/main/AGENTS.md) before work.

The accepted target decision is [ADR-2026-10-16-OWNER-ARCHITECTURE-DECISION.md](https://github.com/berkah-pos/Berkahtigaputeri/blob/main/docs/permanent/ADR-2026-10-16-OWNER-ARCHITECTURE-DECISION.md); the canonical five-layer workbook/configuration contract is [DOC_00](https://github.com/berkah-pos/Berkahtigaputeri/blob/main/docs/permanent/DOC_00_CANONICAL_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md); the target gates are [DOC_14](https://github.com/berkah-pos/Berkahtigaputeri/blob/main/docs/permanent/DOC_14_KVM2_ISOLATED_TENANT_ARCHITECTURE.md); phase order is the [master roadmap](https://github.com/berkah-pos/Berkahtigaputeri/blob/main/docs/permanent/DOC_00_MASTER_ROADMAP.md).

Do not treat Supabase-specific instructions elsewhere in this historical copy as current target-runtime requirements. Supabase sources and data must be retained as current-main implementation/migration evidence until the canonical owner-approved, verified cutover/retirement gates pass. An accepted ADR is not implementation, a green partial workflow is not aggregate CI acceptance, and neither is production deployment evidence.
